    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for saying that. it's just hard when it feels like the art and the feeling are becoming the same thing. i've been thinking about how most people's work is just noise to distract from the void, but maybe the real masterpiece only happens when you actually lean into it. like, if you stop fighting the emptiness and just let it take over. does that even make sense? as a writer, i feel like i'm stuck in this loop of pretending everything is okay when it's clearly not.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
